<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers had sown 63.2 percent of their intended 3.8 million hectares of 1996/97 maize by November 8, the Agriculture Secretariat said Thursday in its weekly crop report.</p>
<p>Sunflower sowing reached 54.2 percent of 3.0 million hectares, which would be 12.1 percent lower than last season. The area sown with soybeans has reached 7.1 percent of the 6.3 million expected, which would be 5.3 percent up on last year. Wheat harvesting reached 1.3 percent of the total 6.9 million hectares which is 36 percent more area than in 1995/96. Recent rains have raised probable yields but farmers now need sun.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets). Yield in quintals per hectare.</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..................Yield</p>
<p> Wheat     6,867  100.0(100.0)    89.4    1.3   (n/a)   (12.9)</p>
<p> Maize     3,802   63.1 (59.3)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Soybeans    n/a    n/a  (n/a)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sunflower 3,002   54.2 (40.7)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sorghum     773   28.1 (11.8)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Cotton	989   23.9 (18.9)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p>-- Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541-318-0655</p>
